From 917daae2377cc3388801ce7f9b41ab2783b7d24d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:33:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 117/117] Preset navigation with every preset in the song
 already changes nothing: no i009, no E058

When the whole instrument is to be replaced (arranger view, song view, a
Clip with an arranger instance), LoadInstrumentPresetUI::doPresetNavigation()
looks for a preset not in the song (Availability::INSTRUMENT_UNUSED). After
going round its list twice without one, its guard against an endless loop
returned one in the song anyway. The arranger's (and the song grid's)
Song::navigateThroughPresetsForInstrument() gave it to replaceInstrument(),
which froze with i009; a Clip with an arranger instance went to it by
changeInstrument() without its instances, and the check after the change
froze with E058 (the fuzzer's seed 226, stop run 9). It now gets out
without a result, as when the list is empty: nothing changes.

Test (beta-1.3/tests/repro/presets_all_used_emu.py): new clips until no
unused preset is left, every clip stopped, then in arranger view a synth
row's audition pad held and the select encoder turned: the row keeps its
synth (before: i009).
---
 src/deluge/gui/ui/load/load_instrument_preset_ui.cpp | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/deluge/gui/ui/load/load_instrument_preset_ui.cpp b/src/deluge/gui/ui/load/load_instrument_preset_ui.cpp
index d0633619..efceb88f 100644
--- a/src/deluge/gui/ui/load/load_instrument_preset_ui.cpp
+++ b/src/deluge/gui/ui/load/load_instrument_preset_ui.cpp
@@ -1564,9 +1564,15 @@ doneMoving:
 	toReturn.fileItem = (FileItem*)fileItems.getElementAddress(i);
 
 	bool isAlreadyInSong = toReturn.fileItem->instrument && toReturn.fileItem->instrumentAlreadyInSong;
-	// wrapped is here to prevent an infinite loop
-	if (availabilityRequirement == Availability::INSTRUMENT_UNUSED && isAlreadyInSong && wrapped < 2) {
-		goto moveAgain;
+	if (availabilityRequirement == Availability::INSTRUMENT_UNUSED && isAlreadyInSong) {
+		// wrapped is here to prevent an infinite loop
+		if (wrapped < 2) {
+			goto moveAgain;
+		}
+		// Every preset there is in the Song already: none to change to. The callers can't take one in use: the
+		// arranger's replaceInstrument() froze with i009, and a Clip with an arranger instance went to it without its
+		// instances (E058)
+		goto noErrorButGetOut;
 	}
 
 	toReturn.loadedFromFile = false;
